From 1826cdcb6dc20d43051a3472233540a1443c23c0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: forge-shepherd <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 9 Jul 2026 10:41:22 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] feat(issues): human-readable handles (title-slug + short-id)
 for at-a-glance tracking
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Opaque UUIDs make it hard to tell what an issue is or track where an agent is across
sub/dependency tasks. Adds issueHandle() = <title-slug>-<8char-short-id> (e.g.
add-oauth-login-56a3a16d): shown in forge ready/list (ID column) and write confirmations
at a TTY. Resolvable — forge show <handle> / <short-id> / even a stale slug + right id all
resolve, because the resolver reads the trailing 8-hex short id (slug is display sugar).
Canonical id stays the full UUID; short legacy/imported ids (forge-2a3bc9, <8 hex) pass
through unchanged with no extra lookup. Verified end-to-end. (kernel 1db53c60)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
